From: gtguerreiro-max <295622337+gtguerreiro-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:12:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/55] gpu: transcendental shader results rounded to 21
 mantissa bits

EXP, LOG, LOGC, RCP, RCPC, RCPF, RSQ, RSQC, RSQF and SQRT results are rounded to 21 mantissa bits,
halfway away from zero, and RCP and RSQ go through DIV and SQRT so the host's own approximations
are not rounded twice (ReduceFloatPrecision; Xenia canary 3a44f20, which fixed Ace Combat 6's
ground, 4E4D07D1, without its vertex index hack). Xenos's exact precision and midpoint rounding
are still not known; Inf, NaN and signed zero stay as the host gives them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../xenos/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator.h   |  3 +
 .../pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator_alu.cpp   | 56 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

